# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers; Windows CRLF line endings would break them ("/bin/sh^M: not found").
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files are never line-ending converted. PDFs above all: their cross-reference table stores byte offsets,
# so turning LF into CRLF (core.autocrlf on Windows) corrupts them.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
